# Nervlith

The product name is Nervlith. Its formal name is Mint Gate. On introductions — a page lead, a document title, a first explanation — write Nervlith (formally Mint Gate). Leave the logo, navigation, and repeated mentions as Nervlith.

Tagline: Build · Govern · Belong. A CKB-native DAO launcher that replaces a centralized forum with cells the chain can verify.

A community is a gate fee plus a governance model. Paying the fee mints a membership card. The card is rendered in the browser from on-chain metadata. It is not an image stored on a server.

Identity is DID:CKB via `@ckb-ccc/did-ckb` (create, resolve, profile, rotate, deactivate, migrate from did:plc). That DID is the passport across communities.

Build phases, the MVP boundary, and which phases are done live in the project-path rule. Follow that status list. Do not build a phase whose box is still open ahead of the current one unless asked.

Constraints:

- Contracts are `no_std` Rust on `ckb-std`. No `std`, no C unless asked.
- Every transaction declares `cellDeps` for the scripts it uses.
- Use the same witness slots (such as `input_type`) in Rust and TypeScript.
- The UI is a dark SaaS shell with a restrained cyberpunk signal: charcoal canvas, orange only for actions and glow. Follow the design-system rule.
- Split a feature across modules. One component, builder, or validation per file. Do not grow a page or a `main` into the whole feature.
